  <entry>
    <id>https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/153.4.0esr/releasenotes/</id>
    <title type="html">Thunderbird 153.4.0esr</title>
    <author>
      <name>Thunderbird</name>
      <uri>https://www.thunderbird.net</uri>
    </author>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/153.4.0esr/releasenotes/"/>
    <updated>2026-09-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <published>2026-09-29T00:00:00+00:00</published>

    <content type="html"><![CDATA[
      

  
  

  
    

    
      
        
        

        
          <h3>Changed</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>RNP command-line utilities are no longer included with Thunderbird</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thundermail built-in add-on updated to v2.0.16</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        
          </ul>
        

        
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Ctrl+Shift+K could fail to open the Quick Filter UI</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Nested S/MIME signed parts could fail to render</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird could hang when waiting for IMAP server greeting during account setup</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Gmail OAuth2 authentication could intermittently fail on Windows</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p><code>AppUpdatePin</code> policy did not prevent Thunderbird from updating beyond pinned version</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>"What's New?" linked to Release channel notes instead of ESR release notes</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p><a href="https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/security/known-vulnerabilities/thunderbird/#thunderbird153.4">Security fixes</a></p>
          
        </li>
      
    
    </ul>
  
  

<p>As always, you’re encouraged to <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">tell us what you think</a>, <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird">ask for help</a>, or <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Thunderbird">file a bug in Bugzilla</a></p>
<style> li p { display: inline; } </style>
      ]]>
    </content>
  </entry>
  
  <entry>
    <id>https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/157.0/releasenotes/</id>
    <title type="html">Thunderbird 157.0</title>
    <author>
      <name>Thunderbird</name>
      <uri>https://www.thunderbird.net</uri>
    </author>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/157.0/releasenotes/"/>
    <updated>2026-09-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <published>2026-09-29T00:00:00+00:00</published>

    <content type="html"><![CDATA[
      

  
  

  
    

    
      
        
        

        
          <h3>What’s New</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Enterprise policy <code>DisableChat</code> disables Thunderbird Chat functionality</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Enterprise policy <code>DisableFileLink</code> disables Thunderbird FileLink functionality</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        
          </ul>
        

        
          <h3>Changed</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Preference <code>mailnews.headers.minNumHeaders</code> has been removed</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Allow viewing remote content in OpenPGP messages encrypted with integrity protection</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>RNP command-line utilities are no longer included with Thunderbird</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>IMAP/POP manual config port field is now optional</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thundermail built-in add-on updated to v2.0.16</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        
          </ul>
        

        
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Ctrl+Shift+K could fail to open the Quick Filter UI</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Message list could show the wrong sender for messages</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Status bar could remain active and cause 100% CPU usage after activity ended</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>OpenPGP discovery failed to find replacement keys after a key was revoked</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Valid RSA OpenPGP keys could be rejected, preventing encryption</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Sent messages could silently fail to save to the IMAP Sent folder</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Sending message did not fail gracefully with malformed references header</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird could hang when waiting for IMAP server greeting during account setup</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Account Hub account creation could fail with malformed URI</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Custom OAuth Endpoint Host incorrectly required a full URL instead of a domain</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Message filters could falsely match when evaluating search term failures</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>CardDAV address books could fail to sync when no password prompt was needed</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Yahoo emails appeared blank with MIME handlers disabled via <code>mailnews.display.disallow_mime_handlers</code></p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Pending moves within the same IMAP account could make messages disappear</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Inline images could disappear after editing and resaving drafts</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>SMTP OAuth2 failed when large access token exceeded command line length limit</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Gmail OAuth2 authentication could intermittently fail on Windows</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Exchange NTLM authentication failed when updated passwords were not saved</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>SMTP AUTH LOGIN could fail after username challenges and close the connection</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p><code>AppUpdatePin</code> policy did not prevent Thunderbird from updating beyond pinned version</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Recurring events could appear after their configured end date</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>CalDAV task body could remain outdated after syncing changes from another client</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>CalDAV invitations could fail when accepted before the calendar synced</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Visual and UX improvements</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p><a href="https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/security/known-vulnerabilities/thunderbird/#thunderbird157">Security fixes</a></p>
          
        </li>
      
    
    </ul>
  
  

<p>As always, you’re encouraged to <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">tell us what you think</a>, <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird">ask for help</a>, or <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Thunderbird">file a bug in Bugzilla</a></p>
<style> li p { display: inline; } </style>
      ]]>
    </content>
  </entry>
  
